# windows/ci/asio-sdk.env: where the ASIO build of PortAudio gets its sources (read by windows/ci/build-portaudio-asio.sh). docs/port/asio-licence.md says why and what follows from it.
# the SDK is NOT in this repository: the build clones it from Steinberg's own repository and ships it, with its LICENSE.txt, in the source folder of the ASIO zip only (GPLv3 option).
# the first CI run (run 42914929737): github.com/steinbergmedia/asiosdk is NOT a public repository (git asked for a user name). the mirror below is a third-party copy of the SDK: its LICENSE.txt is what is
# shipped and checked, but it is not Steinberg's own file (docs/port/asio-licence.md). ASIO_SDK_REPOS are tried in order.
ASIO_SDK_REPOS="https://github.com/audiosdk/asio https://github.com/steinbergmedia/asiosdk"
PA_REPO=https://github.com/PortAudio/portaudio
PA_TAG=v19.7.0
# pins: the commit that the tag / the SDK's default branch must be at. EMPTY = not pinned yet: the build then prints the commit it used (PINNED? lines in the step log and in PA-ASIO-BUILD.txt) and
# these two lines are filled in from that output. a pin that does not match stops the ASIO build (the default WASAPI build does not depend on it).
PA_COMMIT=147dd722548358763a8b649b3e4b41dfffbcfbb6 # v19.7.0, printed by the first CI run
ASIO_SDK_COMMIT=
